 "exclusions": {
  "jr or jalr to an address with bit 0 set: the profile has neither MIPS16e nor microMIPS, so the address is kept and the Address Error exception belongs to the fetch of the target; Unicorn 2.1.4 treats bit 0 as the instruction-set mode bit and clears it": 86,
  "jr or jalr to an address below 0xC0000000 with bit 1 set and bit 0 clear: the Address Error exception belongs to the fetch of the target; the Linux build of Unicorn 2.1.4 reports that fetch as UC_ERR_READ_UNALIGNED before the jump completes, while the Windows build completes the jump": 55,
  "jr or jalr to an address in 0xC0000000 to 0xFFFFFFFF: Unicorn 2.1.4 translates these kernel segments through its TLB model and reports the failed fetch of the target as UC_ERR_READ_UNMAPPED, which the harness cannot tell apart from a fault of the jump itself": 40
 },
